.policy "ruff-n801-invalid-class-name" revision 3
.description "Name classes in CapWords style, starting with a capital letter and without underscores between words, as PEP 8 recommends."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N801 (pep8-naming): a class name that, with its leading underscores taken off, does not start with an
// uppercase letter or still contains `_`. The name is read NFKC-normalised and cased by Unicode, as Ruff reads it.
// Names matching `pep8-naming.ignore-names` are exempt.
//   class bad_class: ...       ← N801
//   class _Good: ...           not reported: leading underscores are allowed
//   class Ｅrror: ...           not reported: it is `Error`
#include "python/python-19.rerail"

.violation N801(at: node, x: symbol) code "N801"
    "Rename class `{x}` to CapWords, such as `MyClass`, and update its references; keep the name if callers outside this code import it."
    suppress ruff "N801"
N801(nm, x) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "name", nm), pep8_name(nm, x), !pep8_capwords(nm, x), !pep8_ignored(nm, x).
